#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:8971
msgctxt "orders-comms"
msgid ""
"When you enter the lounge, you see a guy sitting at the bar with an eye "
"patch, a peg leg, a cutlass at his belt, a three-cornered hat and a green "
"bird on his shoulder."
msgstr "When you enter the lounge, you see a guy sitting at the bar with an eye patch, a peg leg, a cutlass at his belt, a three-cornered hat and a green bird on his shoulder."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:8977
msgctxt "orders-comms"
msgid "Ask about the eye patch, hat, peg leg and bird"
msgstr "Ask about the eye patch, hat, peg leg and bird"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:8984
#, lua-format
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Why, I'm a pirate, matey! Marcus the pirate! Actually, I'm just playing the "
"part of a pirate in the live production of 'Caribbean Pirates' here on %s. "
"I'm on a ten-minute rehearsal break. This stuff I'm wearing is my costume. "
"The peg leg is a hologram and the bird is a robot. I think the bird has "
"better lines than I do.\n"
"\n"
"If you want to talk to real modern pirates, that couple over there at that "
"table are the real deal. They recently retired from a successful career as "
"pirates, or so I hear. This will probably be the only time you can talk to "
"them."
msgstr "Why, I'm a pirate, matey! Marcus the pirate! Actually, I'm just playing the part of a pirate in the live production of 'Caribbean Pirates' here on %s. I'm on a ten-minute rehearsal break. This stuff I'm wearing is my costume. The peg leg is a hologram and the bird is a robot. I think the bird has better lines than I do.\n\nIf you want to talk to real modern pirates, that couple over there at that table are the real deal. They recently retired from a successful career as pirates, or so I hear. This will probably be the only time you can talk to them."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:8991
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Talk to pirate couple"
msgstr "Talk to pirate couple"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:8996
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Hi there, take a seat with us. Marcus signaled us that you've got some kind "
"of interest in pirates. Is that right?"
msgstr "Hi there, take a seat with us. Marcus signaled us that you've got some kind of interest in pirates. Is that right?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9002
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Yes, I want to know about pirates"
msgstr "Yes, I want to know about pirates"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9008
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Well, we can tell you about it. Not that we would ever engage in such "
"practices ourselves."
msgstr "Well, we can tell you about it. Not that we would ever engage in such practices ourselves."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9014
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Of course. How would one get loot from another ship?"
msgstr "Of course. How would one get loot from another ship?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9020
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Loot?! We'd prefer to call that excess cargo. [they laugh at their own "
"joke]\n"
"\n"
"Several things have to come together in order to relieve them of their "
"excess cargo."
msgstr "Loot?! We'd prefer to call that excess cargo. [they laugh at their own joke]\n\nSeveral things have to come together in order to relieve them of their excess cargo."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9026
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "What things have to come together?"
msgstr "What things have to come together?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9032
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Things your ship has to do and things that have to happen on the ship you're "
"liberating excess cargo from. Your ship has to be within 3 units of the "
"other ship, it has to be at a complete stop, it has to have the shields "
"down, it has to have room in the cargo bay, and it has to have at least 50 "
"units of energy per cargo item to operate the transporters that grab the "
"cargo."
msgstr "Things your ship has to do and things that have to happen on the ship you're liberating excess cargo from. Your ship has to be within 3 units of the other ship, it has to be at a complete stop, it has to have the shields down, it has to have room in the cargo bay, and it has to have at least 50 units of energy per cargo item to operate the transporters that grab the cargo."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9038
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "What about the other ship?"
msgstr "What about the other ship?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9044
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Assuming you haven't destroyed it (a common mistake with inexperienced "
"pirates), the other ship has to be completely immobile and their shields "
"have to be down. It also helps if they actually have excess cargo to "
"liberate."
msgstr "Assuming you haven't destroyed it (a common mistake with inexperienced pirates), the other ship has to be completely immobile and their shields have to be down. It also helps if they actually have excess cargo to liberate."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9050
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we know if they have any cargo?"
msgstr "How do we know if they have any cargo?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9056
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Sometimes you can just ask them. Otherwise you can double scan them. You "
"should see the cargo manifest in the ship description. You may have to click "
"the tactical widget or the systems widget on the science console to see the "
"description."
msgstr "Sometimes you can just ask them. Otherwise you can double scan them. You should see the cargo manifest in the ship description. You may have to click the tactical widget or the systems widget on the science console to see the description."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9062
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we get them to stop?"
msgstr "How do we get them to stop?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9068
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Your weapons officer can focus beams on their impulse engines. Once they're "
"in the negatives for their impulse engines, they won't be able to move. If "
"you've double scanned them, your science officer can check the status of "
"their impulse engines by clicking the tactical or description widget and "
"selecting systems.\n"
"\n"
"Now, some freighters have jump drives. You may need to disable those, too. "
"If you don't have beams, you have to use your missiles very carefully to "
"keep from destroying them altogether. You can't get cargo once they're "
"destroyed."
msgstr "Your weapons officer can focus beams on their impulse engines. Once they're in the negatives for their impulse engines, they won't be able to move. If you've double scanned them, your science officer can check the status of their impulse engines by clicking the tactical or description widget and selecting systems.\n\nNow, some freighters have jump drives. You may need to disable those, too. If you don't have beams, you have to use your missiles very carefully to keep from destroying them altogether. You can't get cargo once they're destroyed."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9074
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we get their shields down?"
msgstr "How do we get their shields down?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9080
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"First, shoot them down, then target the applicable shield generator to keep "
"them down."
msgstr "First, shoot them down, then target the applicable shield generator to keep them down."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9086
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Is that it?"
msgstr "Is that it?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9093
#, lua-format
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Once you meet all those requirements, your Relay or Operations officer "
"should see buttons to get cargo from the ship.\n"
"\n"
"Once you go down this path, there's no going back. If you stick to "
"liberating cargo from enemies of the %s, you'll only be called Licensed "
"Privateers. Loot neutrals or friendlies and you'll be labeled Pirates."
msgstr "Once you meet all those requirements, your Relay or Operations officer should see buttons to get cargo from the ship.\n\nOnce you go down this path, there's no going back. If you stick to liberating cargo from enemies of the %s, you'll only be called Licensed Privateers. Loot neutrals or friendlies and you'll be labelled Pirates."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9101
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "What do we do with the excess cargo?"
msgstr "What do we do with the excess cargo?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9107
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Sell it to stations that want to buy it. In fact, you should identify what "
"stations want what goods before you start liberating excess cargo from "
"innocent freighters."
msgstr "Sell it to stations that want to buy it. In fact, you should identify what stations want what goods before you start liberating excess cargo from innocent freighters."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9113
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "How do we find out what stations want goods?"
msgstr "How do we find out what stations want goods?"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9119
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid ""
"Talk to them. Near the end of their status report, they'll say what goods "
"they sell and what goods they'll buy."
msgstr "Talk to them. Near the end of their status report, they'll say what goods they sell and what goods they'll buy."

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9125
msgctxt "pirate-comms"
msgid "Thanks for your help"
msgstr "Thanks for your help"

#: scripts/scenario_44_defenders_or_pirates.lua:9131
